Bloomberg: "The Nvidia Corp. board’s surprise move to reinstate ousted Chief Executive Officer Jensen Huang was done without consulting the company’s senior leaders, who were informed of the plan at the last minute, according to people familiar with what happened. The decision was made Sunday afternoon after board members faced pressure from US President Donald Trump... The plan to bring back Huang, announced shortly before markets opened in New York on Monday, came together in mere hours on Sunday. The deliberations involved Trump but excluded interim CEO Colette Kress and other top executives"

